    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Clarification Request (Specific)"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 94468,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94468.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think the first thing is that you treat people like humans, like the way you would want to be treated. Like, I mean, it is terrible the way that it's impacting lives. And like, as a mom, you know, as like, I can't imagine what it's like. Some of my constituents have lost multiple family members in the same week. And so I think you just, you know, it is like the human, like human scale, you know, connection. And I think on a policy level, like you take them seriously. Like, there is a real problem here. And this was one of the reasons that I was clear that I thought the Biden administration was not meeting their obligations to secure the border and end the flow of fentanyl.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "People should be treated like humans.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "The current situation is having a severe negative impact on people's lives.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a serious problem regarding fentanyl flows at the border.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Some constituents have lost multiple family members within the same week.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The Biden administration has failed to meet its obligations to secure the border.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The Biden administration has failed to stop the flow of fentanyl.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Treating others as one would wish to be treated is a valid moral standard.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Personal experience as a mother gives credibility to emotional responses about loss.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Fentanyl-related deaths are preventable through effective border security policies.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Policy decisions should be based on human-scale impacts rather than abstract metrics.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker’s constituents’ experiences represent broader national suffering.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "Public officials have a duty to respond meaningfully to crises affecting citizens.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Assert / Elaborate"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 94468,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94468.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "You told in New York Times last week that A, or the fundamental mistake politicians make, is condescension. What are examples of that in practice? What have you seen or heard?",
