    "turn_text": "put a ribbon on it. You know, they want to put a ribbon on it to make me, you know, and I'm like, actually, I'm very proud of working in the trades. I'm really proud of fixing things. I think this is, this is the core of pragmatic environmentalism. This is this is being a part of your community. Like, so yeah, you know, and just, they'll try to like, I think they, there was not the anticipation, like I would have something substantive to say. I'm not a cardboard cutout, you know, like I, you know, I have a different set of experiences and, and, and you know, I passed the second most number of amendments of any freshmen in my whole class last year because I have a different set of experiences. Like I'm thinking about what a bill might do to you know, the only grocery store in a rural community or what it would do to, you know, our schools that have already cut down to a four day school week because of budget shortfalls. Like I have a different set of perspectives and experiences and that means that I'm not like competing for the same turf as the 80 lawyers in DC. Like there's a strategic advantage of having a different worldview to bring to the table.",
