      {
        "text": "The significance of passing amendments may reflect strategic negotiation ability or policy impact beyond bill sponsorship.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "First-time members of Congress who pass many amendments likely demonstrate early engagement and credibility.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "The listener values or expects recognition of amendment activity as noteworthy within congressional discourse.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      },
      {
        "text": "There is an established understanding in political circles that amendment success correlates with legislative competence.",
