  {
    "episode_id": 94468,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94468.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. I mean, that was one of the big reasons that I ran for Congress. You know, I was realistic about the chances of actually winning the seat, but I thought I could at least elevate this issue that I see as, you know, nickel and diming the middle class out of existence. making us rely on a cheap set of, you know, of, of goods. So a right to repair basically means that you have the right to fix your own stuff. You bought it, you can fix it. But companies like John Deere Tractor, they put in their terms of service contract that you cannot, you can't wrench on your own tractor. You have to take it to an authorized dealer. And, you know, they all blitzed out at one time and there aren't enough dealers, you know, in the whole country to get all those tractors serviced in time to cut hay. before it turns into something worthless, before it rains. And we've seen it in our business where I used to do a light bulb and a headlight for $3. Now the part is the $700 for the whole assembly. And it's like wiping out. people's savings accounts,",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "I ran for Congress because I wanted to elevate the issue of the middle class being financially burdened by small costs.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "Right to repair means individuals should be able to fix products they legally own.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The issue of rising repair costs is affecting the financial stability of the middle class.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "John Deere's terms of service prohibit owners from repairing their own tractors.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "A single headlight assembly now costs $700, compared to previously replacing just the bulb and headlight for a much lower cost.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "There are insufficient numbers of authorized John Deere dealers nationwide to meet repair demand in a timely manner.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Delayed tractor repairs result in crops becoming unusable due to weather conditions.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "High repair costs are eroding personal savings among consumers.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Consumers who purchase durable goods have moral and practical rights to modify or repair them without corporate interference.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Corporate control over repair processes harms economic fairness and undermines consumer autonomy.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Economic well-being depends on affordable maintenance and repair options for essential tools and equipment.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The current system disproportionately impacts rural and agricultural communities due to geographic disparities in service access.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Consumers trust that ownership implies control, including the ability to maintain and repair purchased property.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Companies like John Deere act strategically rather than altruistically when restricting repair rights.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "Public awareness and political action are necessary to counteract corporate power in repair-related policies.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Assert / Elaborate"
  },
