  {
    "episode_id": 94468,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94468.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "Well, I mean, I think they're looking for different things and the national than, you know, in their rap, like, you know, their state. But I think that, like, for me, you know, it is about really showing up and doing the work and having a sense of agency. And, you know, one of the things I've talked about is that, you know, I think rural America and the trades have suffered bitterly under single party control and It's necessary to have that. If somebody feels entitled to your vote, they're not going to work. I mean, the number of casework successes we've had, I think I've closed 1,600 constituent cases. We've returned $3 million to constituents through casework that money that was owed to them by a federal agency. I take that really seriously. And, you know, I've never been somebody that, you know, my dad's not going to like write an email and give me a job. Like I've had to hustle and people are seeing me hustle and really take it as an honor to get to do this work and work diligently. But yeah, I mean,",
